<article class="env-lemma" id="0FLX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FLX">Lemma <span data-tag="0FLX">50.3.2</span>.</a> Let $p : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. If $p$ is quasi-compact and quasi-separated, then $Rp_*\Omega ^\bullet _{X/S}$ is an object of $D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ S)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      There is a spectral sequence with first page $E_1^{a, b} = R^ bp_*\Omega ^ a_{X/S}$ converging to the cohomology of $Rp_*\Omega ^\bullet _{X/S}$ (see Derived Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/015J" data-tag="015J">13.21.3</a>). Hence by Homology, Lemma <a href="/tag/0132" data-tag="0132">12.25.3</a> it suffices to show that $R^ bp_*\Omega ^ a_{X/S}$ is quasi-coherent. This follows from Cohomology of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01XJ" data-tag="01XJ">30.4.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>